#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:5
#: 4b73626231524806af4996a994aee247
msgid "Analog Airspeed Sensors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:7
#: b7e135148ef245e19eb67eaa4d33255e
msgid "Analog airspeed sensors are becoming hard to obtain, since digital sensors are now as inexpensive and much more accurate and stable. Use of a digital airspeed sensor, versus an analog sensor is highly recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:9
#: a49bcd20f4f045cea86eb24d9087e4ce
msgid "The way this airspeed sensor works is that the top tube is “active” (measures air pressure from the pitot tube that is open at the front and has air driven into it by airspeed) and the bottom one is “static” (measures ambient air pressure from tube with intakes on the side)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:11
#: 60cdc22bb96944eb8ede9d51fe92f157
msgid "Connect the active sensor port using silicon tube to the straight tube exiting from the rear of the pitot tube. The angled tube is the static part connecting to the static port of the sensor (the port on the sensor closest to the PCB)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:13
#: 664842cadf0942be89e5a073fb90a86c
msgid "Set the :ref:`ARSPD_TYPE<ARSPD_TYPE>` to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:16
#: 912f80f9a3d34a409ee0f159f5bf1339
msgid "PX4/Pixhawk Analog Airspeed Pin and Wiring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:18
#: 39e104437c284b5ab2caa9fa668a9a0b
msgid "For the PX4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:20
#: 3b53e8c4d76c420bb186bf81274c7981
msgid "Hardware PIN 11 is available on the PX4 for airspeed use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:21
#: 50531a36549f46c29a48037d2cacae64
msgid "The \"airspeed\" pin 11 is located on a 3 pin DF13 connector on the PX4IO board but is directly connected to the ADC on the PX4FMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:23
#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:45
#: f74b0fe321b649faba49bdfb0b496114
#: 312a00d9502949e1a373a84d044184d4
msgid "This pin can take voltages up to 6.6V (it has an internal voltage divider)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:25
#: 48353759a2d34f6194c492ac3147e220
msgid "The FMU-Pres (air pressure) 3 pin connector is on the end of the PX4IO board opposite the power in connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:28
#: e7e4a6d7ec144703b9ed83f12d83fa51
msgid "Wire the airspeed sensor's signal wire to pin 2 (the center pin) of the FMU-PRES connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:30
#: 61594f57124f4dc7b4d94d4254db4876
msgid "Wire pin 1 (towards the center of the board) to the sensors VCC (5 volts) input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:32
#: 92dcce36312845c19db8d0f6506e062e
msgid "Wire pin 3 (nearest the edge of the board) to the airspeed sensors ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:35
#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:57
#: 89275f9180624247a85e7a26cc8121a0
#: 672de438d2cb4844947ec56f38625d63
msgid "Assign the airspeed sensor to an appropriate \"PIN\" in Mission Planner - Configuration - Advanced Params - Adv Parameter List."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:38
#: d725ba1cb76847f9be1849314416dfc1
msgid "Set the :ref:`ARSPD_PIN <ARSPD_PIN>` parameter to 11 in the Advanced Parameter List and select \"Write Parameters\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:41
#: cf89a35539484f6d9b44e848dccb2052
msgid "For the Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:43
#: c071c00a5fb4451da6ff7e1652440ba5
msgid "The \"airspeed\" pin 15 is located on a 3 pin DF13 connector on the Pixhawk board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:47
#: 0d35771ba4f44110a979fd6020dfd255
msgid "The air pressure connector (labeled ADC 6.6V) is a 3 pin connector on the top right of the Pixhawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:50
#: bd05ba7bc9814086adeb42b9a6da2150
msgid "Wire the airspeed sensor's signal wire to pin 2 (the center pin) of the connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:52
#: 2b9aba4d522b43b8b65f8578135fc5e7
msgid "Wire pin 1 (towards the center of the board) to the sensor's VCC (5 volts) input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:54
#: 8a79907186b34392b959a057f0080971
msgid "Wire pin 3 (nearest the edge of the board) to the airspeed sensor's ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:60
#: 75d30da5fb90416e9cb146139bd58ae8
msgid "For Pixhawk v1, set the :ref:`ARSPD_PIN <ARSPD_PIN>` parameter to 15 in the Advanced Parameter List and select \"Write Parameters\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:62
#: a27177c324a8405bb078b56a670c1c51
msgid "For Pixhawk v4, set the :ref:`ARSPD_PIN <ARSPD_PIN>` parameter to 4 in the Advanced Parameter List and select \"Write Parameters\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:65
#: ee2a3fc1eebd4815ae1227f66543ef9d
msgid "For other  autopilots:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:67
#: 862490070816449e8026c9d006840afe
msgid "Many have an analog RSSI input pin that can serve as the analog airspeed sensor input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:69
#: a19e72f0f05140118858b2501cfb83a1
msgid "Most analog sensors output a signal from 0 to 5V, but most RSSI inputs are 3.3V maximum. If you will never exceed ~60% of the sensor's maximum speed output (normally ~ 200mph for 5V), you will not exceed that rating. However, if you might or just want to be absolutely safe, you can use a 2:1 resistive voltage divider on the signal before applying to the autopilot RSSI input pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:72
#: 2aa99a5d9c7249a88d101369af1f9630
msgid "Once you have the airspeed sensor connected, you can use it to control aircraft speed in auto modes. Change the \"Cruise\" setting in the Tuning screen of either APM Planner (shown) or Mission Planner:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:80
#: c3beed3bfc5e475ea5ce03be5eda057c
msgid "Using a different pin for the airspeed sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:82
#: 9973ac9dcab844549f45586c1d2495b0
msgid "To assign the airspeed sensor to a specific pin, hook up your autopilot to your PC via USB. Start Mission Planner and select the **Connect** button on the upper right of the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:84
#: 33728493f810452f89d54c4396312d1c
msgid "Select the *Configuration* tab then **Advanced Params** and then the **Adv Parameter List**. Scroll down the list to the :ref:`ARSPD_PIN <ARSPD_PIN>` parameter and select the pin you wish to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:88
#: a3a0629e807e4593a8bfe7275994e3bb
msgid "Set this to 0..9 for the APM2 analog pins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:89
#: d3a5a331f9b74f2bb2e40ca1275f7164
msgid "Set to 64 on an APM1 for the dedicated airspeed port on the end of the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:91
#: 54bc5d54444f49fbadf7d9a6a855f250
msgid "Set to 11 on PX4 for the analog airspeed port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:92
#: dc12c2ecc9484abe8d097dc6763a5c57
msgid "Set to 65 on the PX4 for an I2C airspeed sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:93
#: 63ca9659fadd42eb82c350df6868301e
msgid "Set to the listed RSSI pin in other board's :ref:`documentation<common-autopilots>`,often it is pin 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:95
#: 376674b9ca87492eb266bf70c86078f9
msgid "After you have selected the pin, select the \"Update Parameters\" tab and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:96
#: b5ab5ba5d7e349458d896ce4e1c2601b
msgid "close *Mission Planner*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/analog-airspeed-sensors.rst:98
#: 5236e40141064abfb8cdbc44342f04a1
msgid "Additional information on setting the airspeed sensor pin can be :ref:`found here <ARSPD_PIN>`."
msgstr ""
